## Lore

Heavy Machines are the Warlords'' front-line cyborgs: eight to twelve feet of
armored, human-shaped war machine bristling with obvious weapons. They trade
speed, agility and any chance of passing for human for a bigger, stronger
body, heavy armor and firepower.

Most come to identify with the machine. Converted young, they think of
themselves as living weapons and of their old lives as a half-remembered
dream, keep mostly to other cyborgs, and are honored in the War Camps as
patriots who gave up their humanity to defend it. A sculpted face does not
age, so a cyborg of any age may look twenty. A few in a hundred come to hate
what they are, and those are the ones who turn cruel.

## GM Notes

The body is the `warlord-heavy-machine-cyborg` vessel row: 270 M.D.C. main
body, head 100, arms 100, legs 125, forearm weapons 25 each. Robotic P.S. is
typically 28-35 and P.P. 20-24; set them when the character is built.

Pick one Military Specialty at creation: three skills from a single category
(Communications, Espionage, Military or W.P.), each at +15%, whether or not
the category is otherwise open to the class.

Starting kit beyond what the sheet lists: all the ammunition and equipment
for the body''s weapon systems and one weapon with four extra E-Clips for each
W.P. Maintenance and repairs are free in a Warlord''s service. Money is
2D6x100 credits plus 6D6x10 in tradeable goods; pay is 1,300-1,600 credits a
month by rank and record.

A cyborg jet pack, a vehicle and more weapons may be issued by assignment. A
Heavy Machine with no Warlord behind him starts with one less weapon, one
less head feature and no Gromeko identification computer.

A cyborg is thought able to live 200 years with maintenance; in this war the
average is 30 to 50.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'warlord-heavy-machine');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'warlord-heavy-machine';

